{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race telemetry or Evaluator feedback yet, so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract. Geometry: five line sensors spaced 0.02 m apart across x (-0.04 to +0.04 m), placed 0.05 m ahead of the axle so steering reacts before the wheels reach a bend. Sensor footprint is 0.012 m, which is smaller than the 25 mm tape and gives a clean on/off reading. Wheel track 0.12 m and body width 0.12 m keep the off-track limit at max(0.06, 0.0125+0.03)=0.06 m. Wheel radius 0.03 m, mass 0.8 kg and body length 0.18 m are mid-range. Controller: base_speed 1.6 (PWM about 3276) aims for the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed to finish within 3 s, with some margin for turns. Weights are scaled to ±1 with a centre zero, so the signal stays within ±1 and kp=3 gives at most about 1050 PWM of steering difference. That is firm but not saturating. kd=0.15 damps oscillation without amplifying sensor noise much. ki=0 avoids integral windup on the curved course. line_loss 'last_direction' keeps the robot turning toward where the line was last seen. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with the main risks being overshoot in the slalom and speed being too low to finish in time. The observation request asks for every metric so the next iteration can separate speed limits from steering error. Hypotheses to test: (1) 1.6 base speed is enough to finish under 3 s; (2) kp=3 is stable without oscillation; (3) line losses are rare with 0.04 m sensor spread.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.15,
    "sensor_weights": [-1.0, -0.5, 0.0, 0.5, 1.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "Iteration-0 baseline: five sensors at 0.04 m spread, base speed 1.6, kp 3, kd 0.15, no integral term. Built from the contract, not from race data, which does not exist yet. Requests all metrics to diagnose speed and steering next round."
    }
  }
}
